<ReportItem port="443" svc_name="www" protocol="tcp" severity="2" pluginID="104743" pluginName="TLS Version 1.0 Protocol Detection" pluginFamily="Service detection">
<cvss3_base_score>6.5</cvss3_base_score>
<cvss3_vector>CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:L/A:N</cvss3_vector>
<cvss_base_score>6.1</cvss_base_score>
<cvss_vector>CVSS2#AV:N/AC:H/Au:N/C:C/I:P/A:N</cvss_vector>
<description>The remote service accepts connections encrypted using TLS 1.0. TLS 1.0 has several cryptographic design flaws, and PCI DSS has required it to be disabled since June 2018. Modern clients support TLS 1.2 and 1.3.</description>
<plugin_name>TLS Version 1.0 Protocol Detection</plugin_name>
<risk_factor>Medium</risk_factor>
<see_also>https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8996</see_also>
<solution>Enable support for TLS 1.2 and 1.3, and disable support for TLS 1.0.</solution>
<synopsis>The remote service encrypts traffic using an older version of TLS.</synopsis>
<xref>CWE:327</xref>
<plugin_output>TLSv1 is enabled and the server supports at least one cipher.</plugin_output>
</ReportItem>
<ReportItem port="443" svc_name="www" protocol="tcp" severity="2" pluginID="142960" pluginName="HSTS Missing From HTTPS Server (RFC 6797)" pluginFamily="Web Servers">
<cvss3_base_score>6.5</cvss3_base_score>
<cvss3_vector>CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N</cvss3_vector>
<description>The remote web server does not send the Strict-Transport-Security header defined by RFC 6797. Without it, browsers may contact the site over plain HTTP, which allows downgrade and SSL-stripping attacks by anyone on the network path and weakens protection against cookie hijacking.</description>
<plugin_name>HSTS Missing From HTTPS Server (RFC 6797)</plugin_name>
<risk_factor>Medium</risk_factor>
<see_also>https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6797</see_also>
<solution>Configure the remote web server to use HSTS.</solution>
<synopsis>The remote web server is not enforcing HSTS, as defined by RFC 6797.</synopsis>
<plugin_output>
  HTTP/1.1 200 OK
  Server: nginx/1.18.0
  Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8
  Connection: close

The remote HTTPS server does not send the HTTP
"Strict-Transport-Security" header.
</plugin_output>
</ReportItem>
