<ReportItem port="25" svc_name="smtp" protocol="tcp" severity="1" pluginID="54582" pluginName="SMTP Service Cleartext Login Permitted" pluginFamily="Misc.">
<cvss_base_score>2.6</cvss_base_score>
<cvss_vector>CVSS2#AV:N/AC:H/Au:N/C:P/I:N/A:N</cvss_vector>
<description>The remote SMTP server advertises that it allows cleartext logins (AUTH PLAIN or AUTH LOGIN) over an unencrypted connection. Anyone able to watch the traffic can read the credentials.</description>
<plugin_name>SMTP Service Cleartext Login Permitted</plugin_name>
<risk_factor>Low</risk_factor>
<see_also>https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4954</see_also>
<solution>Configure the service to offer authentication only after STARTTLS, or to use an encrypted mechanism.</solution>
<synopsis>The remote mail server allows cleartext logins.</synopsis>
<xref>CWE:319</xref>
<plugin_output>The SMTP server advertises the following SASL methods over an unencrypted channel :

  All supported methods : LOGIN, PLAIN
  Cleartext methods     : LOGIN, PLAIN</plugin_output>
</ReportItem>
<ReportItem port="3389" svc_name="msrdp" protocol="tcp" severity="2" pluginID="58453" pluginName="Terminal Services Doesn't Use Network Level Authentication (NLA) Only" pluginFamily="Misc.">
<cvss3_base_score>4.8</cvss3_base_score>
<cvss3_vector>CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:N</cvss3_vector>
<description>The remote Terminal Services is not configured to use Network Level Authentication (NLA) only. NLA authenticates the user before a full RDP session is set up, which protects the server against denial of service and against attacks that need a session, and lets the client check the server's identity first.</description>
<plugin_name>Terminal Services Doesn't Use Network Level Authentication (NLA) Only</plugin_name>
<risk_factor>Medium</risk_factor>
<see_also>https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/remote/remote-desktop-services/clients/remote-desktop-allow-access</see_also>
<solution>Enable Network Level Authentication (NLA) on the remote RDP server, under the Remote settings tab of System Properties.</solution>
<synopsis>The remote Terminal Services doesn't use Network Level Authentication only.</synopsis>
<plugin_output>Nessus was able to negotiate non-NLA (Standard RDP Security) security.</plugin_output>
</ReportItem>
