<ReportItem port="3389" svc_name="msrdp" protocol="tcp" severity="3" pluginID="42873" pluginName="SSL Medium Strength Cipher Suites Supported (SWEET32)" pluginFamily="General">
<cvss3_base_score>7.5</cvss3_base_score>
<cvss3_vector>CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N</cvss3_vector>
<cvss_base_score>5.0</cvss_base_score>
<cvss_vector>CVSS2#AV:N/AC:L/Au:N/C:P/I:N/A:N</cvss_vector>
<cve>CVE-2016-2183</cve>
<description>The remote host supports SSL/TLS cipher suites of medium strength: those with keys from 64 to 112 bits, or that use the 3DES suite. 64-bit block ciphers such as 3DES are vulnerable to the SWEET32 birthday attack on long-lived connections, and an attacker on the same network can break medium-strength encryption far more easily than strong encryption.</description>
<plugin_name>SSL Medium Strength Cipher Suites Supported (SWEET32)</plugin_name>
<risk_factor>High</risk_factor>
<see_also>https://sweet32.info
https://www.openssl.org/blog/blog/2016/08/24/sweet32/</see_also>
<solution>Reconfigure the affected application, if possible, to avoid use of medium strength ciphers.</solution>
<synopsis>The remote service supports the use of medium strength SSL ciphers.</synopsis>
<xref>CWE:326</xref>
<plugin_output>
  Medium Strength Ciphers (&gt; 64-bit and &lt; 112-bit key, or 3DES)

    Name                          Code             KEX           Auth     Encryption             MAC
    ----------------------        ----------       ---           ----     ---------------------  ---
    DES-CBC3-SHA                  0x00, 0x0A       RSA           RSA      3DES-CBC(168)          SHA1

The fields above are :

  {Tenable ciphername}
  {Cipher ID code}
  Kex={key exchange}
  Auth={authentication}
  Encrypt={symmetric encryption method}
  MAC={message authentication code}
  {export flag}
</plugin_output>
</ReportItem>
